[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/tests/dependency_solver_impl_test.py: Resolve coverage feedback: add test_resolve_rolls_back_failed_dependency_subtree, where the highest-precedence 'app' candidate introduces two new unassigned constraints (extra, lib >=5.0.0) and the lib subtree has zero viable releases; the search must roll back both merged constraints and the candidate assignment before selecting the next 'app' release, which then resolves to app/extra/lib at 1.0.0. This exercises backtracking rollback over a failed dependency subtree (missing spans 183-185, 189). Cleared the addressed feedback projection from the metadata block.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: Fix range parsing: compound clauses now bind operators occurring after whitespace separators so '>=1.0.0 <2.0.0' compiles to conjunctive GE 1.0.0 and LT 2.0.0, and full bounds are validated against local SemVer 2.0.0 grammar so bare partials '1', '1.2', '>1.2', '^0.0', '1.2 - 2.3', '<=1' always raise InvalidRangeError independently of collaborator parsing
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/dependency_solver_impl.py: Remove the unreachable conflict-explanation fallback so a failed dependency search always reports the accumulated conflict trail, since every failing branch records a diagnostic before backtracking
