[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/tests/dependency_solver_impl_test.py: Resolve coverage feedback: add test_resolve_candidate_exhaustion_raises_conflict, where every candidate of the top-level 'app' package has a viable version range but its dependency subtree fails (highest candidate needs a missing 'ghost' package, lower candidate needs lib >=5.0.0 with no viable release). The search must roll back each failed subtree and, after exhausting all candidates, report a ResolutionConflictError with the involved packages. This exercises the candidate-exhaustion-under-unsatisfiable-subtree branch (missing span 189). Cleared the addressed feedback projection from the metadata block.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: Prune defensive dead code from range compilation per coverage feedback: drop the unused _RangeTarget.is_wildcard property, make the tilde expansion the explicit default after the simple and caret operator cases, collapse the wildcard upper-bound helper to only its reachable one- and two-component cases, and remove the redundant tokenizer position guards; also drop the unexercisable InvalidVersionError catch around collaborator parse_version since local SemVer grammar validation already guarantees acceptance
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver_multi/tests/semver_range_impl_test.py: Resolve coverage feedback with six new RangeEngine tests: malformed wildcard component placement raising InvalidRangeError (1.x.3, x.1.2, 1.*.2, 1.2.x.4, >=1.x.3); caret upper bounds on zero-major and wildcard prefixes (^0.2.3 -> <0.3.0, ^0.0.3 -> <0.0.4, ^0.x, ^0.0.x); wildcard relational upper/lower bounds (>1.x, >=1.x, <1.x, <=1.x, >1.2.x); '!=' wildcard and comparator exclusions (!=1.x, !=1.2.x, !=1.5.0); unsatisfiable comparator conjunctions (>2.0.0 <1.0.0); and the universal '>=*' wildcard. Cleared the addressed feedback projection from the metadata block.
